  "id": "symbiotic-relationship",
  "term": "symbiotic relationship",
  "definition": "In cognition, a symbiotic relationship is a mutually shaping link between structural brain connectivity and brain activity, where each influences the other. In the source context, this two-way interaction is described as important for the development and self-organization of complex brain networks.",
